{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>For the tribe of Reuben, etc.</b> Scripture listed the tribes neither by their standards, nor by their hosts, nor by their genealogies. It appears that he saw fit to list them here according to the rank of the emissaries, for they were heads and princes of the people, as he related, and their rank is not equal — rather, among them one is greater than his fellow in wisdom and in honor. And he gave precedence to the most honored, preceding in rank, for by their own personal rank he listed them, not by the rank of the tribe. And so too with the princes who would apportion to them the land of Canaan (below 34:17–29), he mentioned them according to rank, not by their genealogies."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:04:39.952610743Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}